meta {
  name: Sync Branch Lab Tests
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/branch-lab-tests/sync
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "listId": "{{branchLabTestListId}}"
  }
}

tests {
  test("201/200", function () {
    expect([200, 201]).to.include(res.getStatus());
  });
  test("reports created/updated/deleted/failed", function () {
    const data = res.getBody() && res.getBody().data;
    expect(data).to.have.property("created");
    expect(data).to.have.property("updated");
    expect(data).to.have.property("deleted");
    expect(data).to.have.property("failed");
  });
}

docs {
  **Reconcile** a branch's Lab Test List against its Branch Master Data, scoped to
  one pricing list. Send `{}` to reconcile the whole list, or
  `"branchLabTestIds": ["<id>", ...]` to restrict it to a subset.

  `listId` (optional) targets a specific `BranchLabTestList` — must belong to the
  caller's branch (404 `BRANCH_LAB_TEST_LIST_NOT_FOUND` otherwise). Omit it to
  sync the branch's default **Walk-in** list, which is always ensured to exist
  first regardless of which list `listId` targets.

  **Reconcile semantics** (Master Data is the source of truth):
  - **UPDATE** — an existing imported original is re-snapshotted (parent fields +
    clinical `configSnapshot` overwritten; branch-level edits discarded).
  - **DELETE** — an imported original whose source no longer exists in Master Data
    is soft-deleted (a sibling is promoted to default if needed).

  Sync does **not** ADD — adding a Master Data test to a list is "Import from
  Master Data". So `created` is always 0. User duplicates (`isDuplicate=true`) are
  never touched. Writes commit in batches and a failing batch is counted and
  skipped so the rest still runs → result `{ created, updated, deleted, failed }`.

  This is the synchronous endpoint (also the FE's fallback). For live progress use
  the background job: `POST /branch-lab-tests/sync/jobs` (see "Start Sync Job").
}
